  "the container gate is name equality plus one alias step (x = P; x[k] = v).  It is not an alias proof: two names can point at one object through a parameter default, a module global, or a call that returns a shared dict, and none of those are followed",
  "an 'unresolved' domain beside an open container gate is the only state in which this face cannot answer, and the verdict names that limit rather than folding it into either answer",
